From 8f39026e0e68ebbfe834943f499280bda0f0ed21 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Filippo Falezza <filippo.falezza@outlook.it>
Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 17:03:11 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 47/69] backlight: qcom-wled: Don't enable the OVP IRQ twice

When the bootloader leaves the module enabled, wled_configure_ovp_irq()
keeps the OVP interrupt enabled but wled->brightness stays 0, so the
first non-zero brightness calls wled_module_enable() again and the OVP
work enables the interrupt a second time ("Unbalanced enable for IRQ").
Track the module as on in that case.

This patch was generated by an AI coding assistant (Claude Opus 5.5 in
Claude Code) during an interactive bring-up session on a Motorola Moto G
5G Plus (XT2075-3, "nairo"). It has not yet been reviewed line by line
by a human and needs that review before any submission.

Assisted-by: LLM dtschema
---
 drivers/video/backlight/qcom-wled.c | 7 +++++++
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/video/backlight/qcom-wled.c b/drivers/video/backlight/qcom-wled.c
index 129d64409..6bcf9c546 100644
--- a/drivers/video/backlight/qcom-wled.c
+++ b/drivers/video/backlight/qcom-wled.c
@@ -1651,6 +1651,13 @@ static int wled_configure_ovp_irq(struct wled *wled,
 	/* Keep OVP irq disabled until module is enabled */
 	if (!(val & WLED3_CTRL_REG_MOD_EN_MASK))
 		disable_irq(wled->ovp_irq);
+	else
+		/*
+		 * The bootloader left the module on with the irq enabled:
+		 * track it as on, so that the first non-zero brightness does
+		 * not enable the irq a second time.
+		 */
+		wled->brightness = 1;
 
 	return 0;
 }
